+# Playtest script: FinLit Street prototype slice (15 min)
+
+**Who:** Moses + Noa (9, design anchor) — or any kid 8+.
+**What:** the prototype on this branch (`game/` Godot project), portrait window.
+**Goal:** validate the spec's acceptance criteria before any further spend. This
+is the *gate*, not a demo — watch more than you talk.
+
+## Setup (before the kid arrives, 2 min)
+
+1. Run the game: `godot --path game` (or open `game/project.godot` in the Godot
+   editor and press ▶). Delete any prior save for a true first launch:
+   `user://finlit_save.json` in the app-userdata folder.
+2. Have this page + a pen ready. Note the clock.
+
+Observer rules: **no helping, no explaining**. If the kid asks "what do I do?",
+answer "what do you think you do?" — comprehension must come from the game.
+
+## Minute 0–2 — First launch & the life lottery
+
+Kid sees: age pick → street name card → life lottery → empty street → one
+glowing **FIND WORK** button.
+
+Watch & note:
+- [ ] Age pick: instant or hesitant? Which bracket?
+- [ ] Street name: did they mash 🎲 NEW NAME (fun) or accept immediately?
+- [ ] **LIFE LOTTERY REACTION — the key read.** If they rolled "A Friend's
+      Couch": did it read as *cartoonish hard luck with a path forward* or as
+      *unfair/sad*? Quote their exact words: ______________________
+- [ ] Did they try the disabled 🎲 REROLL button? (Evidence for the OPEN
+      reroll-policy question — note whether its absence frustrated them.)
+- [ ] Did they find and tap FIND WORK without prompting? Time: ______ s
+
+## Minute 2–5 — First job & first wage (acceptance row 1)
+
+**Criterion: within 60 seconds — circumstances rolled, job taken, first wage
+received, zero reading beyond 3-word labels.** Time it: ______ s · PASS / FAIL
+
+Watch & note:
+- [ ] Job choice: which one, and *why* (ask after: affection vs pay)? Dogs
+      predicted the affection pick.
+- [ ] Reaction to the first wage (coin blip + balance bump): did they notice?
+      Did they smile / comment? This is the juice moment.
+- [ ] Did they read anything aloud or stumble on a label longer than 3 words?
+
+## Minute 5–12 — The core loop (acceptance rows 2 & 3)
+
+Let them play unaided. The street should pull them: BUY glows when affordable.
+
+- [ ] Bought ≥2 assets? Which? Did the generated names land ("Sunny Duplex")?
+- [ ] Upgraded once? Did they notice the building grow / level stars?
+- [ ] Survived one event? If a 🔧 Burst Pipe hit: **can the kid say what it
+      cost THEIR building?** Ask: "what just happened to your duplex?" —
+      looking for "I had to pay $X to fix it" (teach-through-consequence).
+      Their answer: ______________________
+- [ ] If a 📈 Rate Hike landed with no debt: did the "no effect" beat make
+      sense to them? Any comment?
+- [ ] Did they tap ❓ (the Mrs. K help button)? Scripted answer or, if
+      `DEEPSEEK_API_KEY` was set, the LLM one — ask which they preferred if
+      you ran the 🐞 debug compare: ______________________
+- [ ] Did they open 🏆 the league panel? Reaction to the YOU row (wealth
+      *climbed*)?
+- [ ] Any moment of confusion, boredom, or "what do I do now?" Note it with
+      the time: ______________________
+
+## Minute 12–15 — The wrap questions (acceptance row 3 + D1 read)
+
+Ask directly, neutrally:
+1. "Want to play again tomorrow?" — **the D1-return question.** YES / NO.
+   If no: what would make it a yes? ______________________
+2. "Show me your street." — do they narrate ownership ("this is MY snack
+   cart, it pays me")? That's the ownership-formula test passing out loud.
+3. "Was anything unfair?" — lottery read #2, post-play.
+4. "What would you buy next?" — forward desire = loop health.
+
+## Scoring the gate (fill after)
+
+| Acceptance criterion | Evidence | PASS / FAIL |
+|---|---|---|
+| Minute one: lottery + job + wage ≤60s, ≤3-word labels | time above | |
+| Disaster teach: kid states what it cost *their* building | quote above | |
+| Unaided: ≥2 assets, 1 upgrade, 1 event survived, asks to play tomorrow | ticks + Q1 | |
+
+**Open-question evidence for canon:**
+- Reroll policy (OPEN): ______________________
+- No-parents tone (sensitivity): ______________________
+- LLM tutor vs scripted (integrate-vs-drop): ______________________
+
+Anything surprising at all → write it down; it goes into the next spec revision.
